  "response": "# Hotspot triage for `04-monorepo`\n\nEvery finding has `churn: 0` and `recency: 0`, so the scan has no change-frequency data. This order is based only on code structure and test coverage. Where a finding shows `test_gap: 0.75`, the code has no direct tests. Write characterization tests there before refactoring.\n\n## The hotspots\n\n| File | Fan-in | Fan-out | Transitive importers | Size findings | Tested? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/utils.ts` | **18** (p99 = 10) | 1 | **26** | 424-line file | yes |\n| `src/index.ts` | 4 | **17** (p99 = 11) | 4 | 459-line file; `build` 293, `<anon>` 274, `mainTasks` 194, `normalizeOptions` 96, `startWatcher` 79, `buildAll` 75 | yes |\n| `src/esbuild/index.ts` | 1 | **11** (= p99) | 4 | `runEsbuild` 237 lines, reads 38 option keys | yes |\n| `src/plugin.ts` | 10 (9 of them types only) | 3 | 16 | `buildFinished` 103 | **no** |\n| `src/log.ts` | 9 (4 types only) | 0 | **30** | none | **no** |\n| `test/utils.ts` | 9 | 0 | 9 | none | n/a (test helper) |\n| `src/rollup.ts` | **0** | 7 | 0 | `getRollupConfig` 122 | **no** |\n| `src/api-extractor.ts` | 1 | 6 (= p95) | 4 | `rollupDtsFiles` 85 | **no** |\n\n## Refactor order\n\n**1. `src/index.ts`: the biggest tangle and the safest place to start.**\n- Fan-out is 17, well above the p99 cutoff of 11. Five of its functions break the size limit, and `build` is 4.9× the threshold. Most of `build`'s body is the 274-line anonymous function, and most of that is `mainTasks` (194 lines).\n- Only 4 files import it (fan-in 4, transitive 4), so changes inside it barely reach callers. It also has tests (`test_gap: 0`).\n- The plan: pull `normalizeOptions`, `buildAll` and `startWatcher` out into their own modules, and keep `build` as a thin coordinator. This also spreads its 17 imports across smaller modules, so each one depends on fewer things.\n- While doing this, fix `build`/`buildAll`. Their names sound like they have no side effects, but both call `removeFiles`.\n\n**2. `src/esbuild/index.ts`: same idea, one level down.**\n- Fan-out is 11, right at p99. Only one file imports it, and it has tests.\n- `runEsbuild` is 237 lines (4.0×) and reads 38 different keys from one `options` object. Splitting that object into named, narrowly typed groups (plugins, define/env, output) is what makes it possible to break up the function.\n- The two `Date.now()` calls on lines 98 and 278 can move behind an injected clock at the same time.\n\n**3. `src/utils.ts`: the largest blast radius, so fix its tests before touching the code.**\n- 18 files import it directly and 26 transitively, the most of any non-leaf module. It's also 424 lines (1.4× the 300-line limit). Every edit here currently reaches 26 files.\n- **Prerequisite:** 12 weak-test findings are scored against `src/utils.ts` as the code under test (crime_00009, 17, 18, 30, 31, 35, 36, 43, 44, 56, 65, 70). One test has no assertions at all; the rest use only weak matchers. Strengthen those tests first. Until then, a passing suite tells you little about this file.\n- **How to split:** move each group of functions into its own module, and keep `utils.ts` as a re-export barrel so none of the 18 importers have to change. Then move importers to the narrower modules gradually.\n- Also fix `jsoncParse` (lines 135–139), which silently returns `{}` when parsing fails. Make it throw or return a result callers can check.\n\n**4. `src/plugin.ts`: only `buildFinished`.**\n- `buildFinished` is a 103-line class method. Its 16 transitive importers make it the second-largest runtime blast radius on this list, and it has no tests. Add tests first, then extract helpers.\n- Leave the rest of the file alone. 9 of its 10 importers only import types, so that coupling exists at compile time only. Being widely imported is the purpose of a shared type module.\n\n**5. Later, when you're already editing these files:**\n- `src/esbuild/postcss.ts`: `postcssPlugin` 140 / `setup` 126, 7 transitive importers, no tests.\n- `src/cli-main.ts`: `main` 153 lines, but only 2 importers.\n- `src/esbuild/svelte.ts`: 116 / 106 lines, has tests.\n- These are long functions, but few files depend on them. Refactoring them makes those files easier to read but doesn't shrink anyone else's blast radius.\n\n## Leave alone\n\n- **`src/log.ts`**: 30 transitive importers, the most in the repo, but its only finding is that connectivity. Fan-out is 0 and there are no size findings. A logger is meant to be imported everywhere, and restructuring it would affect 30 files to fix nothing. Treat it as load-bearing.\n- **`test/utils.ts`**: fan-in 9 because 9 test files share it, which is its job. The one real issue, an unbounded `Promise.all` over `fsp.mkdir`/`writeFile` (lines 38–46), is a small fix that doesn't need a restructure.\n- **`src/rollup.ts`**: fan-in 0, so its blast radius is zero and refactoring it reduces nobody else's risk. `getRollupConfig` (122 lines, a misleading name, no tests) is worth cleaning up only when someone is already working in that file.\n- **`src/api-extractor.ts`**: fan-out 6 exactly equals the p95 cutoff, fan-in is 1, and `rollupDtsFiles` is only 1.4× the threshold. Low priority.\n- **`swcTarget` / `terserPlugin` (62 lines) and `swcPlugin` (65 lines)**: all about 1.0–1.1× the threshold, which is close enough to be noise.\n\n## In one line\n\nBreak up the two high-fan-out coordinators first (`index.ts`, then `esbuild/index.ts`). They're tested and few files depend on them, so it's cheap. Then strengthen the tests for `utils.ts` and split it behind a barrel, because it's the module whose changes reach the most files. Don't restructure `log.ts`, the type imports from `plugin.ts`, or the test helper. Being widely imported is their job, and changing them would affect many files to fix nothing.",
